Fix out-of-bounds packet access and unsafe libpcap capture handling
Validate captured packet lengths before accessing DHCP and ARP headers
or copying packet data. Use pcap_pkthdr.caplen to prevent reads beyond
captured data and reject truncated or oversized packets.
Copy DHCP payloads into a properly sized structure to avoid out-of-bounds
access warnings with GCC 16. Validate UDP payload lengths, including
the minimum DHCP header and magic cookie size.
Also prevent outgoing packet buffer overflows and ensure capture timers
are cancelled on both success and error paths.
